--TEST--
The three PHP programs the side-by-side section of the PHP-differences chapter shows do not compile, and `$_GET` is refused by naming the `Core` member that replaces it — `rule:classes/no-free-functions-or-constants`, `rule:statements/no-host-populated-variables`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: tools:php-differences/two-spellings-side-by-side
// The section shows three programs, one per code it names. This case holds
// them in one file, in the section's order, so one compile reports all three.
function total(array $xs) {
    return array_sum($xs);
}
echo total([1, 2]) === 3 and true;

class Point {
    public function __construct(public int $x, public int $y) {}
}

string $name = $_GET["name"];
echo (int)$name;
